{"findings":[{"finding":"REQ-1 requires Google-only sign-in, while the accepted ASM-12 says to use email/password and explicitly says there is no social sign-in or SSO, leaving mutually exclusive authentication requirements.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-18 relies on a vehicle being marked as having a permanent parking sticker, but no requirement defines how that marker is recorded or maintained, so the stated verification bypass has no specified setup path.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-15 defines the concurrent last-space failure but gives no acceptance behavior for a claim submitted when availability is already zero, including the error and refreshed availability response.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-21 allows security to record actual entry but does not specify or test that only authorized guards can submit or change that outcome.","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-24 permits administrators to remove recipients, including potentially the entire list, but REQ-23 specifies the reporting job only when recipients are configured and gives no behavior for an empty list.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-23 says the report runs on “Monday morning” without defining a time, so the job acceptance criterion cannot establish when the scheduled report is due.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}]}